1ff" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{-e}^{0}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x=A,$ what is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb02ea64c6406af5947f6735f7e3abbac6f894588bff7df58b5c9ec8c49771ff" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)={e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =({e}^{-x}-{e}^{-(-x)}) \\\\  & =({e}^{-x}-{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)={e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-e}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-e}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-e}^{0}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ A+{\\int }_{0}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x & =-A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb02ea64c6406af5947f6735f7e3abbac6f894588bff7df58b5c9ec8c49771ff" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9c1ec128486d1779cde54681fee1a120288070b2589fe0b7e6859e2636d19e74" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb02ea64c6406af5947f6735f7e3abbac6f894588bff7df58b5c9ec8c49771ff" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-A"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb02ea64c6406af5947f6735f7e3abbac6f894588bff7df58b5c9ec8c49771ff" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-156191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}A"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033652/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb02ea64c6406af5947f6735f7e3abbac6f894588bff7df58b5c9ec8c49771ff" "basis" 1232 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/ques